## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to translate reliability into a product mindset across multiple teams, define measurable outcomes, and design practical experiments that balance speed and quality.

## Key Concepts

- Observability as a product
- SLOs and error budgets
- Instrumentation with OpenTelemetry
- Incident rituals and blameless postmortems
- Toil reduction experiments

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal OpenTelemetry trace init (illustrative)
import { trace } from '@opentelemetry/api';
const t = trace.getTracer('service');
const span = t.startSpan('request');
// business logic
span.end();
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale this program across eight squads? 
- Which metrics would you track beyond MTTR and velocity?

## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to design lightweight governance frameworks for multi-team organizations with regional considerations, emphasizing practical artifacts, rituals, and measurable outcomes.

## Key Concepts

- Engineering governance
- Artifacts and rituals
- Metrics and experiments

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple guardrail filter: decide if a feature request should be evaluated against guardrails
function shouldGuardrailsApply(request) {
  const highImpactPatterns = [/auth|security|data/i];
  return highImpactPatterns.some((r) => r.test(request.description));
}
```
